id: vile-weather
name: Vile Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
profile: elemental-poison
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The poison. Combat Rolls Botch on 2(WT) or lower, Stress Tests roll 1(WT) lower past
  Natural, and at Cataclysmic every Combat Roll is 1(bT) worse.
text: >
  Vile Weather: Poison rains down from the skies or bubbles up from below the surface,
  filling the air with deadly toxin.

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Poison)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * You score a Botch Result for a Combat Roll on a Natural Result of 2(WT) or lower.

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * Reduce the Dice Score of your Stress Tests by 1(WT).

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * Reduce all of your Combat Rolls by 1(bT).

---

# The only Weather that makes a roll go wrong rather than making it worse, which is a
# different kind of cruel: a Botch is not a low number, it is a result with a rule of its
# own attached.
#
# --- Natural (1): the Botch Range ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "You score a Botch Result for a Combat Roll on a Natural Result of 2(WT) or lower."
#
# For a Combat Roll. Not for a Skill Check - a Perception Check made in the poison is no
# likelier to go wrong than one made in clean air - so this writes to `botchRange.combat`,
# which is a second Botch Range that only a Combat Roll is measured against. It was added
# for this.
#
# `min=` rather than `=`. The rule says a Natural Result of 2(WT) or lower is a Botch,
# which is a floor under how easily you botch and not a ceiling: something else that had
# already widened the range further keeps its wider one, and the poison does not make a
# botching character safer.
#
# `min=` is the floor and `max=` is the ceiling in this language - "at least" and "at
# most", not "take the larger" and "take the smaller". Written the other way round first,
# and a ceiling of 2 on a range of 1 changes nothing at all, so it read as the Weather
# simply not working.
#
# 2(WT), so the range is 2 at Natural, 4 at Unnatural and 6 at Cataclysmic - and against a
# Critical Target of 10 that is better than half the die at the top Tier. The derived value
# is held below the Critical Target, so it can never reach a Natural Result that is already
# a Critical.
#
# --- Unnatural (2): the Stress Test -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce the Dice Score of your Stress Tests by 1(WT)."
#
# A Stress Test is 1d10 plus your Stress Bonus, so the Bonus *is* the Dice Score above the
# die - reducing one is reducing the other, and there is no second number for the roll.
#
# Written to `stress.dice` at first, a Slot of its own said on the sheet and applied by the
# table, on the reasoning that nothing here rolls a Stress Test. That was a number invented
# beside one that already existed and did the job, which is how two values end up
# disagreeing about the same thing. The Slot is gone.
#
# So this one is applied rather than said, even though the Test itself belongs to
# Transformations and there are none yet: whenever one is rolled, the Bonus it uses is the
# one on the sheet, and the poison is already in it.
#
# --- Cataclysmic (3): every Combat Roll ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce all of your Combat Rolls by 1(bT)."
#
# All of them, which is what `combatRolls` is: it fans out to the Strike, the Dodge and the
# Wound, so one line reaches all three and a fourth Combat Roll would be reached without
# this file being touched.
#
# (bT) rather than (WT) - written as the rule writes it, and by the top Tier the Botch
# Range is doing the heavy work anyway.
#
# --- What is not built ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Poison)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles,
# and there are none in this system yet. Carried in the header and read by nobody.

[passive]
botchRange.combat min= 2(WT);

if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
  stressBonus -= 1(WT);
}

if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 3) {
  combatRolls -= 1(bT);
}
